    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30-a16">

                <pb facs="0669" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv10/pg659"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>58 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lombard Street,<lb/>London, E. C.</hi> 3</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1919-11-08">Nov. 8,
                    1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Under Secretary of State for
                        Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Office, Downing
                        Street, S.W. 1</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith copy
                    of letter I have received this morning from H. E. Nubar Pacha giving particulars
                    of his interview with Colonel Haskell. Colonel Haskell’s views are doubtless
                    already known to you but they indicate such a serious prospect in Armenia that I
                    venture to express the confident hope that His Majesty’s Government will once
                    more extend their generous assistance to avert the calamity with which such a
                    vast number of Armenians are still threatened.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James A. Malcolm</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
